SUMMARY:Art History in the Afternoon: Marcel DuChamp
LOCATION:Pittsfield Branch: Program Room\, 2359 Oak Valley Dr\, Ann Arbor\
 , MI 48103
GEO:42.2451;-83.7877
DESCRIPTION:The French artist Marcel Duchamp's artistic career spanned six
  decades and included such major art movements as Cubism and Surrealism\,
  as well as being credited with the invention of "readymades" and "assist
 ed readymades"\, but\, ultimately\, Duchamp's work cannot be categorized.
 \n\nWhere: 2359 Oak Valley Dr\, Ann Arbor\, MI 48103\nAges: Grade 6–Adult
 \nCost: Free\nSignup: Drop in\, no signup needed\nIndoors\nListed by: Ann
  Arbor District Library\nDetails: https://aadl.org/node/668665\nFound on:
  https://kideventsinannarbor.com/?event=9a4cf23ffdb6ae79\n\nDouble check 
 the time with the organizer before you go.
URL:https://aadl.org/node/668665
CATEGORIES:Public Event
END:VEVENT
